    <section class="cv-block cv-warn" id="second-chance" aria-labelledby="second-title">
      <h2 id="second-title">How Udemy Second Chance works</h2>
      <p>
        Second Chance is Udemy's retake assurance for AWS vouchers. It is not a separate product you can buy later, and
        it is not an AWS programme. You buy it with the original voucher, and it gives you one extra attempt if you
        fail.
      </p>
      <ol class="cv-steps">
        <li><strong>Buy it with the original voucher.</strong> It cannot be added after checkout.</li>
        <li><strong>Take the first exam through Pearson VUE.</strong> The normal AWS scheduling and ID rules apply.</li>
        <li><strong>If you fail, claim it in My learning → Certifications.</strong> Choose <em>Claim Second Chance</em> before the original voucher expires.</li>
        <li><strong>Udemy verifies the result.</strong> A new voucher code usually arrives within seven days.</li>
        <li><strong>Book the retake with the new code.</strong> The replacement is valid for at least nine months from issuance.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="cv-note">
        One extra attempt only. Non-refundable and non-transferable. If you pass first time, the Second Chance portion
        is not refunded. Do not book the retake until the new code arrives.
      </p>
    </section>

