    <section class="cv-block" id="legit" aria-labelledby="legit-title">
      <h2 id="legit-title">Are Udemy AWS exam vouchers legitimate?</h2>
      <p>
        Yes — with one important distinction. Udemy is the <strong>seller of the voucher</strong>, not the exam
        provider. AWS owns the certification, and Pearson VUE delivers the test. That is why the code is redeemed
        inside the AWS Certification account and Pearson VUE checkout, not inside Udemy.
      </p>
      <ul class="cv-check">
        <li><strong>Who sells it:</strong> Udemy, on udemy.com. The receipt and voucher code come from Udemy.</li>
        <li><strong>Who delivers the exam:</strong> Pearson VUE, AWS's testing provider. You schedule and reschedule there.</li>
        <li><strong>Who issues the certification:</strong> AWS. Udemy cannot issue, renew or verify an AWS certification.</li>
        <li><strong>How to verify your code:</strong> it appears in My learning → Certifications and is accepted at Pearson VUE checkout.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="cv-note">
        Red flags: a seller who asks for a bank transfer, sends a code by direct message, or offers a price far below
        the AWS list price. Vouchers are non-transferable, so a code from a stranger may not work. Buy from the official
        Udemy page or Pearson VUE.
      </p>
    </section>

