        certification, check the <a href="#aws-50-percent">50% AWS discount voucher</a> first — it can beat both Udemy prices.
      </p>
      <h3>When the 50% AWS discount wins</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You already passed an AWS exam and have the voucher in your Benefits section.</li>
        <li>You are planning a second certification: 50% off SAA-C03 is $75.</li>
        <li>You are recertifying an existing certification.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>When the bundle makes sense</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You are attempting a Professional or Specialty exam, where a retake costs $300.</li>
        <li>You have not taken an AWS exam before and want a financial safety net.</li>
        <li>You would rather pay a fixed premium now than risk a second full fee later.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>When paying AWS directly is better</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You are confident and only need one attempt.</li>
        <li>The voucher-only price is higher than the AWS list price.</li>
        <li>You need maximum flexibility on dates or local-currency pricing.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Other legitimate ways to lower the cost</h3>
      <ul class="cv-links-list">
        <li><strong>AWS promotions:</strong> free retakes and exam discounts appear throughout the year. Check <a href="https://aws.amazon.com/certification/bulk-voucher/terms-and-conditions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AWS voucher campaign terms</a> before buying.</li>
        <li><strong>Employer bulk vouchers:</strong> Pearson VUE runs AWS's bulk voucher portal for teams. Ask your employer before paying retail.</li>
        <li><strong>AWS Educate and community programmes:</strong> eligible learners sometimes receive free vouchers; availability and deadlines vary.</li>
        <li><strong>Discounted prep courses:</strong> coupons do not apply to vouchers, but they do apply to courses. A $10–$15 course plus one exam fee is usually the cheapest path.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

